abstract: >-
  Rectangles, solver, checker and paper for 33 improved upper bounds relative to
  the 51 non-square instances in CP 2025 Table 1, with the other 18 matched.
  The mean reduction over improved instances is 18.5%. Final values use up to
  16 allocated CPU minutes per instance. A separate historical experiment has
  a pooled median first-improvement time of 0.12 CPU seconds across 165 runs
  on the 33 improved instances. This is not a controlled cross-study speedup.
  Every rectangle is independently checked with exact arithmetic.
keywords:
  - Latin rectangles
  - spatially balanced Latin squares
  - combinatorial design
  - local search
  - simulated annealing
  - constraint programming
